From: Orange Pi 3 PCIe reference build
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-3: restore PHY rail delay

The board DTS documents that the external RTL8211E Ethernet PHY requires
GMAC-2V5 and ALDO2 to be enabled, followed by a 100 ms settling delay.  The
comment says that reg_aldo2 provides this delay, but the property was omitted
from the Linux 5.7.4 copy of the DTS.  Without it, the initial MDIO scan can
miss the PHY; the MAC module and netdev still register, while ndo_open later
fails when phylink cannot attach to the PHY.

Restore the property already present in the repository's experimental board
DTS and in later Orange Pi 3 board support.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
@@ -259,6 +259,7 @@
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 				regulator-name = "vcc33-audio-tv-ephy-mac";
+				regulator-enable-ramp-delay = <100000>;
 			};
 
 			/* ALDO3 is shorted to CLDO1 */
-- 
